# corpus/ fixtures are byte-exact captures of real tools' `--help` output
# (corpus/README.md). Git's CRLF normalization, "fix trailing whitespace"
# safe-crlf checks, and any editor/formatter that "cleans up" text on save
# must never touch them — the mess in the raw bytes is the test. `-text`
# disables Git's own text handling (autocrlf conversion, diff EOL fixups)
# for everything under this path.
corpus/** -text
